BonVoyage API Gateway native package
================================

This package contains the RouteSphere BonVoyage gateway executable and its
hardened systemd unit. It supplies neither a configuration snapshot, secret
material, control-plane process nor host-tuning policy.

Install a reviewed snapshot at /etc/bonvoyage/snapshot.pb with root ownership,
the bonvoyage group and mode 0640. After verifying configuration and runtime
dependencies, explicitly enable and start bonvoyage.service. The packaged unit
keeps administrative and metrics endpoints on loopback by default.

Runtime logger severity is sent through the local syslog socket to journald.
Raw stdout and stderr are retained at info priority. Ensure /dev/log and
journald are available before starting the service. The package does not alter
host-wide journald, rsyslog, CPU, NUMA, NIC, IRQ, sysctl or power policy.

A fresh installation does not enable or start the service. Upgrades preserve an
operator's prior enabled state, stop a running service and do not start it again
automatically. Perform upgrades in a reviewed maintenance window, verify the
package and snapshot, and then explicitly start the service. Keep the prior
admitted package available for rollback.

Removal and purge retain the service identity, snapshots, secrets, state and
logs. The source-install unit at /etc/systemd/system/bonvoyage.service must be
reconciled before installation; this package never replaces that administrator
unit silently.

A successfully assembled package is only a technical candidate. Verify its
release manifest, SBOMs, vulnerability review, provenance, signature and
lifecycle receipts before installation. Documentation is available at
https://docs.routesphere.global/.
